NAME
       getsebool - show the values of SELinux booleans

SYNOPSIS
       getsebool BOOLEAN...
       getsebool -a

DESCRIPTION
       Booleans are on/off switches in the SELinux policy that allow or forbid
       optional behaviour, for example whether the web server may serve
       users' home directories (httpd_enable_homedirs) or connect to the
       network (httpd_can_network_connect). getsebool prints each one as

           httpd_enable_homedirs --> off

       Change them with setsebool; add -P to keep the change after a reboot.
       semanage boolean -l lists them with a short description and the
       value they have by default.

OPTIONS
       -a     List all booleans.

EXAMPLES
       Find the booleans about home directories:

           getsebool -a | grep home

       Turn one on for good and check:

           setsebool -P httpd_enable_homedirs on
           getsebool httpd_enable_homedirs

SEE ALSO
       setsebool(8), semanage(8), booleans(8)
